# An ENTRY node turned off by a written `_should_flow: false`. Entry
# nodes have no incoming wires, so this is the one branching shape the
# wired-guard fixture (skip/) cannot reach: the decision has to be read
# from the node's own braces at kick time. The rig asserts the node is
# skipped with reason `did_not_flow` (a decision, distinct from the
# consequence `required_input_closed` its consumer gets), its body never
# produced a value, and the run still completes.

gated = Text {
  value: "never produced"
  _should_flow: false
}

out = Debug
out.data = gated.value
